# What is yours about a deployment. `make setup` copies this file to deploy.local.env, and stops
# there the first time: the two hostnames below are yours to choose, and nothing is set up without
# them. deploy.local.env is not committed: the two wrangler.jsonc files keep their example values,
# and `make deploy` puts these into the configs it generates (scripts/deploy-config.ts).
#
# Another deployment in the same Cloudflare account has a file of its own, named after it:
#   make setup DEPLOY_ENV=deploy.team-a.env      writes deploy.team-a.env from this file
# Its name goes on the end of the names of its two Workers and its database: httpdog-house-ui-team-a,
# httpdog-house-ingest-team-a and httpdog-house-team-a. Name that file on every command for it, and
# keep its name: under another one it is another deployment. Start it from this file, never from
# another deployment's file, whose DATABASE_ID is that deployment's.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required: fill these in first
#
# The two hostnames of the deployment, without https://. A deployment is always served from
# hostnames of your own, never from workers.dev.
#
#   UI_DOMAIN       where you sign in             for example alerts.example.com
#   INGEST_DOMAIN   where httpdog POSTs alerts    for example hook.example.com
#                   (the address to give a host is https://<INGEST_DOMAIN>/<INGEST_PATH>/alerts,
#                   with INGEST_PATH from further down)
#
# Each is a name under a domain that is in the same Cloudflare account, and that has no DNS record
# yet: Cloudflare makes the record and the certificate when the Worker is uploaded.
#
# Certificates are logged in public, so a hostname is not a secret: anyone can come across it.
# A name that does not say what it is for gives less away.
UI_DOMAIN=
INGEST_DOMAIN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- filled in by `make setup`
#
# The id of the D1 database both Workers use. `make setup` creates the database and writes it here
DATABASE_ID=

# The last piece of the address to sign in at: https://<UI_DOMAIN>/<ENTRY_PATH>. It is the only
# address of the UI that answers a browser it has not seen; the hostname alone, and everything
# else, answers "not found". `make setup` writes 16 random characters here, unless you put a name
# of your own first: 8 to 64 letters, digits, dashes and underscores, and nothing anyone would
# guess. `make entry` shows the whole address. To change it later, change it here and run
# `make deploy-ui`.
ENTRY_PATH=

# The piece of the receiver's address before /alerts: https://<INGEST_DOMAIN>/<INGEST_PATH>/alerts.
# The receiver takes alerts there and answers "not found" at every other address, so a stranger
# cannot send it anything. `make setup` writes 16 random characters here, unless you put a name of
# your own first, by the same rule as ENTRY_PATH. The keys page shows the whole address for a host.
# Leave it as it is once hosts send to it: changing it means changing it on every host.
INGEST_PATH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional
#
# Settings of the receiver. Empty means the default; after a change, `make deploy-ingest`.
#
# How many days an alert is kept. Older ones are deleted once a day. 0 keeps alerts forever.
# Default 365
RETENTION_DAYS=
# How far a request's timestamp may be from the receiver's clock, in seconds. A request outside it
# is refused as stale, so raise it only for hosts whose clocks cannot be kept right. Default 300
MAX_SKEW_SECS=
